## P3 — How to explore the “content sea”

1. **Start narrow:** `search` with module name + concept (e.g. `Inventory Smart product status sku_status`, `sourcing intermediate MERGE`).
2. **Scope to space when noisy:** CQL `space = IA AND text ~ "product_attributes_filter" AND type = page`.
3. **Walk the tree:** parent page → `getConfluencePageDescendants` → fetch only relevant children (batch if many).
4. **Prefer handbook pages over random comments** for implementation truth.
5. **Cross-check client reference codebase** (`insideinsight-mtp-bigquery` per client-reference rule) when Confluence shows OOTB SQL — Lululemon may differ.
6. **Capture durable learning:** append to `findings/lululemon_knowledge_bank.md` or `Self Notes/`; mirror if the tree will be referenced again.

---

## P4 — Guardrails

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Read pages/issues yourself via MCP | Ask the user to paste Confluence when MCP is available |
| Use markdown format for reading | Default to `updateConfluencePage` / `createConfluencePage` |
| Fetch descendants before assuming a parent body has the content | Assume an index page contains the SQL (often empty — see Sourcing Tables) |
| Note when Confluence links out to Google Sheets / Colab only | Treat a link-only page as fully mirrored |
| Retry once on transient `fetch failed` | Give up after one failure on large trees |

**Writes (Confluence/Jira create/edit/transition):** only when the user **explicitly** asks. Default is read-only exploration.

